+Closes #615.
+
+## What this changes
+
+`/understand` can now run inside a **drive**. A drive is a run of plays that keeps going until its goal is met, then gets reviewed (ADR 029). This is item 6 of the #606 plan, one of the pieces the Kickoff drive (#613) needs. It is the same change #614 made for `/vision`.
+
+- **Handed a drive's contract, `/understand` opens nothing.** It runs no `start-change`, and no commit, propose, review or merge of its own. It works on the drive's branch and still commits its model change there.
+- **It does not wait at its checkpoint.** It renders the checkpoint as it would have been shown, every box-move as its own line, and saves it as a review record in the drive's review folder. Kickoff runs it once per capability, so each run leaves its own record.
+- **Seed answers come from the drive.** For a capability not yet in the model, the what, why and domain come from the contract (`answers.understand.seeds.<capability>`). With none, it stops and asks the person. It never makes them up.
+- **Run by hand, nothing changes.**
+
+## Kapil's choice (recorded in `.garura/project/issues/615/specs/plan.md`)
+
+A box-move raises one of the product's agreed limits and writes a decision. Inside a drive, that decision is written `proposed`, not `accepted`, because no person has said yes. The drive's review accepts or drops it. The save step runs before the checkpoint resolves, so the play decides by "am I in a drive", not by the checkpoint's outcome: every box-move in a drive is `proposed`.
+
+## Where to look
+
+- The intent change: `core/components/plays/understand/reference/ice.md` (new C13, F14, F15, S7, REC14, REC15; C1, C8, C9, C11, C12, F7, REC7 say what changes in a drive). `SKILL.md` was recompiled from it; the fingerprint is refreshed.
+- `persist_understand.py` gains `--decision-status accepted|proposed` (default `accepted`).
+- `check_drive_contract.py` and `write_drive_review.py` are stamped, byte-identical copies of the canonical ones in `play-creator/references/`.
+- `standards/rules/pipeline-position.md` now lists `/understand` as wired for drives.
+
+## Also on this branch
+
+Commit 914cbd6b (the #614 done mark and the #606 plan moving to item 6) was on local main and never pushed. It rides along here; the 606 and 614 plan edits are not part of #615.
+
+## Tests
+
+- All 21 test files under `core/` pass. `test_persist_understand.py`: 46 (7 new, for the decision status). `test_drive_contract.py`: 26, every copy identical.
+- `lint_play` passes on `/understand` (0 gaps).
+- The component lint reports 114 errors, all in files this change does not touch.
+
+## Not in this change
+
+- `/intent` moving to the shared contract checker.
+- The drive's review accepting a `proposed` box-move, or writing the person's real answer back into the checkpoint's learning record (#617 / #613).
+- Breaking the hard chain with `/vision` (its own Story).
